<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY" ;
  triage:title "AI.40 M5 UDS one-frame baseline artifact is a failed/degenerate run and run_admission_capacity.py has no validation gate rejecting a non-conforming baseline" ;
  triage:description "Successor to ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-CHRONOLOGY (chronology sub-claim resolved and closed at 1f6b2cbb). The retained pre-AI.39 baseline artifact reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072313.590684-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json (source_revision fb6b26363c5bb0bbb11a6cf167d090385dc53d35, genuinely pre-AI.39) is itself an invalid measurement: sample_count=1 (sprint doc requires minimum 10), run_duration_s=0.138 (sprint doc requires ~20s), passed=false at both interval and run level, first_failure='HTTP 503: sqlite connection budget exceeded (max 3 concurrent reader handles...)', admissions_per_second=180.94 (far below the sprint's own 1,000/s floor). scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py's load_baseline_median() (lines ~613-631) returns the real numeric median computed from this failed run with no validation of the artifact's own passed/sample_count/run_duration_s fields; evaluate_profile_thresholds() (line 592) then consumes that value directly as `baseline_passed = baseline_median is None or median >= baseline_median`, so a degenerate ~181/s floor trivially passes for any subsequent measurement. baseline_reference() (lines ~634-650) separately surfaces a `passed` boolean as descriptive metadata only -- this is NOT the value consumed by the gate, and is not itself a safeguard. Independently confirmed by quality-mgr via direct read of the raw JSON artifact and the three named functions; independently corroborated in full technical detail (same file:line citations, same raw-artifact fields) by both req-qa (filed as ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY) and arch-qa (filed as ARCH-001, RULE-013) during AI40-QA-4. ruthless-boundary-qa's AI40-QA-4 disposition characterized the `passed:false` field as inert/non-gating metadata and called this fixed; that characterization is factually incorrect -- it conflates baseline_reference()'s descriptive `passed` field with load_baseline_median()'s numeric return value, which is what evaluate_profile_thresholds actually gates on. test_baseline_reference_retains_source_revision_and_observed_result in test_run_admission_capacity.py documents that a passed:false baseline payload is accepted and retained unchanged, with no rejection path -- the existing test suite codifies this gap rather than guarding against it." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-AI" ;
  triage:triageMode "follow_up" ;
  triage:category "acceptance-gap" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file_only" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady true ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:foundIn triage:AI40 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-2> ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "1" .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-1>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py" ;
  triage:line 613 ;
  triage:snippet "STILL OPEN at c73ab129 (AI40-QA-5). load_baseline_median (lines 613-637) now has a real validation gate -- rejects baseline.get('passed', False) is False, sample_count < minimum_sample_count, run_duration_s < target_duration_s -- confirmed present in code by quality-mgr, arch-qa, and req-qa. quality-mgr independently verified the checked-in evidence artifacts contradict the claim that this protects the deliverable: reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072313.590684-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json is itself a self-failed baseline record (source_revision fb6b26363c5bb0bbb11a6cf167d090385dc53d35, passed=false, sample_count=1, run_duration_s=0.138) -- exactly the shape the new gate should reject -- and reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/20260801-072441.255944-mac-arm64-01-uds-f1.json embeds it as its consumed baseline with baseline_median_admissions_per_second=180.94 computed from it, thresholds.baseline_passed=true / top-level passed=true with no failure recorded. PROVENANCE CLARIFIED by arch-ctm (message 01KYY9CFTBT7HSWCQJ1V2P940V, 2026-08-01T09:09:51Z): fb6b2636 genuinely fails M5 at ~25/1000 admissions/s with HTTP 503 reader-budget exhaustion -- this is real pre-fix performance, not a measurement bug. The fixes producing today's passing evidence (14962/s) are descendants of fb6 (4b7c7676 et al.); c73ab129's load_baseline_median correctly rejects fb6's baseline as invalid when freshly evaluated, but the checked-in 20260801-072441 artifact predates c73 -- it was generated by a pre-validation script version and left committed, i.e. this is STALE evidence, not evidence of a broken/bypassed gate. Root open question (not decidable by quality-mgr, escalated to team-lead): arch-ctm states 'a passing pre-AI.39 baseline cannot be regenerated honestly' since pre-AI.39 code genuinely failed the sprint's own floor -- this is a criterion/acceptance-definition question (what satisfies Deliverable 6 when no honest passing pre-AI.39 measurement exists), not a code defect quality-mgr can resolve via QA verdict. Regardless of that policy question, the stale 20260801-072441 artifact must not remain checked in as if authoritative -- it should be regenerated or removed once the criterion is decided." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s40-local-transport-benchmark" ;
  triage:headSha "e514bcc4" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/S40/e514bcc4> .

<urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-40-BASELINE-INTEGRITY/S40-2>
  a triage:Occurrence ;
  triage:file "scripts/smoke/run_admission_capacity.py" ;
  triage:line 613 ;
  triage:snippet "FIXED at e514bcc4 (AI40-BASELINE-FIX-1, verified AI40-QA-6). The narrow scope of this finding -- load_baseline_median's own validation gate, and the checked-in evidence chain that was silently consuming the self-failed fb6b2636 record (20260801-072313...json) as a passing baseline via the now-deleted 20260801-072441...json artifact -- is genuinely resolved: (1) 20260801-072441...json is confirmed absent from reports/benchmark/send-message-benchmark/ (repo-wide grep for the filename and for source_revision fb6b26363c5bb0bbb11a6cf167d090385dc53d35 returns only the retained diagnostic artifact itself); (2) the retained 072313 record is now explicitly labeled evidence_role='pre_fix_diagnostic_not_comparison_baseline' (descriptive metadata only, never read by any code path -- confirmed via grep, dropped on publish per benchmark_report.validate_result); (3) new regression test test_invalid_baseline_is_rejected_before_its_median_is_used (test_run_admission_capacity.py:281-289) calls the real load_baseline_median() with a passed=false/sample_count=1 payload and asserts SmokeError, non-tautological; (4) load_baseline_median is confirmed wired into the live --baseline invocation path (run_admission_capacity.py:820-823, fed from CLI --baseline via profile_baseline for the UDS one-frame profile). Independently verified by quality-mgr (direct grep/read) and corroborated in full by both req-qa and arch-qa during AI40-QA-6. CI green 8/8 legs at e514bcc4 (run 30704100571). The separate acceptance-criterion policy question (whether Deliverable 6's pre-AI.39 baseline requirement can be satisfied at all) was already resolved by the user/team-lead per the AI40-BASELINE-FIX-1 dispatch and is explicitly out of scope for this round -- not re-litigated here. A NEW, structurally distinct finding (unguarded consumption in matching_profile_median(), the sibling TCP-comparison-median path) was surfaced by arch-qa and independently confirmed by quality-mgr during this same round; tracked separately as AI40-TCP-COMPARISON-MEDIAN-UNVALIDATED.ttl since it is a different function, different code path, and was not part of this finding's original scope." ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:closed true ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-08-01T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:branch "feature/pAI-s40-local-transport-benchmark" ;
  triage:headSha "e514bcc4" ;
  triage:occursIn <urn:atm:triage:worktree/S40/e514bcc4> .

